            "review_title": "Review at Cafe Tra Chanh",
            "review_text": "Stanley H\nHong Kong, China11208 contributions\n0\nTraditional Vietnamese Coffee\nDec 2024 • Family\nFor Christmas, the family went to Vietnam. The next day in Hanoi, there was only two hours of free activity. After we visited the old streets of Hanoi, we thought about trying traditional Vietnamese coffee. In the old town, the numerous cafes and restaurants of all kinds make us more confused. Finally, at the gathering point in front of the church, we met this “Trà Chanh 26 Casa Thờ”, which we want to try, is traditional egg coffee and salt coffee. \n\nBecause the gathering time is near, I just rushed to buy two cups of coffee. One of the flavors is the traditional Vietnamese salt coffee Salt Coffee. This is a frozen coffee. Replace sugar with salt. A frozen coffee that makes us breathe is all of the salad aroma.\n\nAnother cup of coffee with a traditional Vietnamese flavor is a hot drink, more so hot food. Because this cup of egg coffee (Egg Coffee) is a cup of coffee that you can eat. Once the lid is opened, the fragrant egg golden aroma intensely spreads out.\n\nSaid, this is a cup of \"eat\" coffee. The store gave us a bowl, a bowl of coffee-filled pulp. And the taste is coffee, a mixture of milk and egg flavor, and aromatic, and intense, and sweet, and nutrient. A wonderful and very special glass of drink or food.\n\nYeah! I haven't tried coffee in a long time to feel full. Two cups of coffee, the main taste sensation is the aroma of salad. Very special. It really is to come to Vietnam in person to get the taste of coffee. After we learned, we only later learned that the name of this shop is Vietnamese lemon tea.\nRead more\nTranslated from Chinese\nShow original\nWritten February 18, 2025",
